Marker only - see CONTRIBUTING.md. build() unsets LD_LIBRARY_PATH (meson's
own tooling crashes the same way other native builds do if it's still
pointed at the sysroot) and package() creates /var/lib/66/system (66 boot
expects it and warns at boot otherwise, doesn't mkdir it itself). package()
also sed-patches /etc/66/init.conf to CATCHLOG=0/VERBOSITY=1 (upstream's
CATCHLOG=1 can hang boot indefinitely in this system's fork/fifo rendezvous;
VERBOSITY=2 prints tree-management chatter over the console) and release=2
is the bump that ships that fix. gen-ports.py must never regenerate over
this - none of the above has a manifest.tsv field.
